an effect row whole (heaven_and_earth_witness): {'en': "heaven and earth called to witness — the STATUS the case's evidence clause writes on Israel: 'I call heaven and earth to witness against you this day that you shall surely perish quickly from the land … you shall not prolong your days upon it but shall be utterly destroyed' (Deut 4:26) — the witnesses of the exile case (4:25-31: corrupt → perish, scatter, few, serve wood and stone; seek → find; return → mercy); the Sifrei 306:1's CHAIN OF WITNESSES — 4:26 the third of eleven (30:19 'I call heaven and earth to witness against you this day', 31:28 'that I may call heaven and earth to witness against them', 32:1 'give ear, O heavens'; 30:19's first seven words identical, computed); 'the end of days' (4:30) a prophecy — no timer, no exile written; Gittin 88a:15-17 and Sanhedrin 38a:6 (the exile hastened by two years of 'grown old'); Megillah 31b:2 (the Ninth of Av's reading)", 'he': 'הַעִידֹתִי בָכֶם הַיּוֹם אֶת הַשָּׁמַיִם וְאֶת הָאָרֶץ (I call heaven and earth to witness against you this day — Deut 4:26)', 'ledger_op': 'status', 'ink': "Deut 4:26 ('I call heaven and earth to witness against you this day'), 4:25 ('when you beget sons and sons' sons and have grown old in the land and deal corruptly'), 4:27-31 (the arms), 30:19, 31:28, 32:1 (the chain — forward); Leviticus 26:33, 26:42 (the tochacha's scatter and remember — the first tellings, by CALL), 28:36, 28:64 (forward); Onkelos 4:26; the Sifrei 306:1 on 32:1 (read at the reading); Babylonian Talmud Gittin 88a:15-17, Sanhedrin 38a:6, Megillah 31b:2", 'corpus': 'deu_04_obey_horeb (STEP_Dt_4_25 through STEP_Dt_4_31; the claim DV04A-04)', 'exam': 'cold_run_obey_horeb.py (F4 the_exile_case — the_case_head, the_witnesses, perish_and_scatter, seek_and_find, in_your_distress_return, the_merciful_god; the tape kind witnesses_called)', 'third_seat': "THE DEUTERONOMY WALK 19b (2026-09-27) — the STATUS REUSED at Deut 30:19 by law_covenant_return_charge on israel_people (the line life_and_death_choice_declared: 'I call heaven and earth to witness against you this day: life and death I have set before you' — its first seven words identical with 4:26; THE CHAIN OF WITNESSES 4:26, 30:19, 31:28, 32:1 — obey_horeb's DATA the_witnesses_chain); 4:26 the first seat, 8:19's 'I testify' the second", 'fourth_seat': "THE DEUTERONOMY WALK 19b (2026-09-27) — the STATUS REUSED at Deut 31:28 by law_covenant_return_charge on israel_people (the line assembly_and_song_spoken_declared: 'assemble to me all the elders of your tribes and your officers, that I may speak these words in their ears and call heaven and earth to witness against them' — the chain's fourth seat; 32:1 'give ear, O heavens' the fifth, sitting 20's)"} | (song_a_witness_against_israel): {'en': "the song a witness against Israel — the STATUS the line song_witness_commanded writes on Israel: 'THAT THIS SONG MAY BE FOR ME A WITNESS AGAINST THE CHILDREN OF ISRAEL … this song shall testify before them as a witness, for it shall not be forgotten from the mouth of their seed' (31:19, 31:21) — 'a witness' (le'ed — patched 'for-a-witness' at the reading's tail; 31:19, 21, 26 the chapter's three seats): THE TWO WITNESSES OF THE CHAPTER — the song and the book (31:26), beside the heavens and the earth (30:19, 31:28) — a DATA row the_witnesses_of_the_chapter; 'testify' patched 'and-shall-testify'; 'not forgotten from the mouth of their seed' the witness's condition (Sanhedrin 21b OWED); satiety before rebellion at 31:20 (8:12-14 — good_land by CALL; 'sated' the seven's homograph guarded)", 'he': 'לְמַעַן תִּהְיֶה לִּי הַשִּׁירָה הַזֹּאת לְעֵד בִּבְנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵֽל (that this song may be for Me a witness against the children of Israel — Deut 31:19)', 'ledger_op': 'status', 'ink': "Deut 31:19-21, 31:26 (this runner's own line — the book a witness), 30:19, 4:26 (obey_horeb — heaven and earth to witness, the reference), 8:11-14 (good_land — satiety before rebellion); Onkelos 31:19-21", 'corpus': 'deu_29_moab_covenant (STEP_Dt_29_1 through STEP_Dt_29_28; claims DV29-01 through DV29-05), deu_30_teshuvah_choice (STEP_Dt_30_1 through STEP_Dt_30_20; claims DV30-01 through DV30-04) and deu_31_charge_torah (STEP_Dt_31_1 through STEP_Dt_31_30; claims DV31-01 through DV31-06)', 'exam': 'cold_run_covenant_return_charge.py (F14 the_song_commanded — that_this_song_be_a_witness_for_me; the line song_witness_commanded) — THE LEAN PASS: the exam the seven Mishnah and Tosefta rows the ledger cites (deu_29_31_nitzavim_vayelech_exam_2026-09-27.md)'} | (song_written_and_taught_by_moses): {'en': "the song written and taught by Moses — the STATUS the line song_written_taught writes on Israel: 'and MOSES WROTE THIS SONG THE SAME DAY AND TAUGHT IT TO THE CHILDREN OF ISRAEL' (31:22) — THE ACT: the fourth of THE FOUR WRITINGS (journeys' DATA by CALL); 'the same day' THE MARKER'S DAY (40, 12, 7) — 31:2's 'this day' and 31:22's 'the same day' one day; the command of 31:19 DONE (a receipt-shaped close without the formula — no register seat); the song in Israel's mouth, its text chapter 32's (sitting 20's)", 'he': 'וַיִּכְתֹּב מֹשֶׁה אֶת הַשִּׁירָה הַזֹּאת בַּיּוֹם הַהוּא וַֽיְלַמְּדָהּ אֶת בְּנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵֽל (and Moses wrote this song the same day and taught it to the children of Israel — Deut 31:22)', 'ledger_op': 'status', 'ink': "Deut 31:22, 31:19 (this runner's own line — the command), 32:44 (the closing frame — sitting 20's); Numbers 33:2, Exodus 24:4 (journeys — the four writings, the reference); Onkelos 31:22", 'corpus': 'deu_29_moab_covenant (STEP_Dt_29_1 through STEP_Dt_29_28; claims DV29-01 through DV29-05), deu_30_teshuvah_choice (STEP_Dt_30_1 through STEP_Dt_30_20; claims DV30-01 through DV30-04) and deu_31_charge_torah (STEP_Dt_31_1 through STEP_Dt_31_30; claims DV31-01 through DV31-06)', 'exam': 'cold_run_covenant_return_charge.py (F14 the_song_commanded — moses_wrote_this_song_that_day; the line song_written_taught) — THE LEAN PASS: the exam the seven Mishnah and Tosefta rows the ledger cites (deu_29_31_nitzavim_vayelech_exam_2026-09-27.md)'} | (face_hidden_and_forsaken_foretold): {'en': "the face hidden and the forsaking foretold — the conditional HEAVEN entry the line apostasy_and_hidden_face_foretold writes on Israel: 'then My anger shall be kindled against them in that day and I WILL FORSAKE THEM AND HIDE MY FACE FROM THEM, and they shall be devoured' (31:17) — THE HIDDEN FACE: Onkelos 'I will remove My Shekhinah' at 31:17, 31:18 and 32:20 (the reading's crown); 'I will hide My face' the form's one seat (32:20 the song's); the face hidden the covenant's negative arm on Heaven's side (glory_appeared the positive — the two faces of one ledger); Leviticus 26:38's devouring the twin (tochacha by CALL); Chagigah 5a-b OWED; 31:18's infinitive absolute 'I will surely hide' (8:19's doubled warning — good_land by CALL)", 'he': 'וַעֲזַבְתִּים וְהִסְתַּרְתִּי פָנַי מֵהֶם (and I will forsake them and hide My face from them — Deut 31:17)', 'ledger_op': 'heaven', 'ink': "Deut 31:17-18, 32:20 (the song — sitting 20's); Leviticus 26:38 (tochacha — devoured, the reference); 8:19 (good_land — the doubled warning); Onkelos 31:17-18", 'corpus': 'deu_29_moab_covenant (STEP_Dt_29_1 through STEP_Dt_29_28; claims DV29-01 through DV29-05), deu_30_teshuvah_choice (STEP_Dt_30_1 through STEP_Dt_30_20; claims DV30-01 through DV30-04) and deu_31_charge_torah (STEP_Dt_31_1 through STEP_Dt_31_30; claims DV31-01 through DV31-06)', 'exam': 'cold_run_covenant_return_charge.py (F13 the_apostasy_foretold — my_anger_kindled_i_will_forsake_them_and_hide_my_face; the line apostasy_and_hidden_face_foretold) — THE LEAN PASS: the exam the seven Mishnah and Tosefta rows the ledger cites (deu_29_31_nitzavim_vayelech_exam_2026-09-27.md)'} | (moses_barred_from_the_land): None | (barred_from_the_land): {'en': "barred from the land — HEAVEN's BLOCK the sentence at Meribah writes on Moses and on Aaron: 'because you did not believe in Me, to sanctify Me in the eyes of the children of Israel, therefore you shall not bring this assembly into the land which I have given them' (Num 20:12); 'Aaron shall be gathered to his people, for he shall not come into the land' (20:24); Aaron's CLOSED by his death (20:28), Moses' OPEN to Deut 34:5; the run citations 27:14, Deut 32:51", 'he': 'לָכֵן לֹא תָבִיאוּ אֶת הַקָּהָל הַזֶּה אֶל הָאָרֶץ (therefore you shall not bring this assembly into the land — Num 20:12)', 'ledger_op': 'heaven', 'ink': 'Num 20:12, 20:24, 27:14; Deut 32:51, 34:5', 'corpus': 'num_20_meribah_edom_aaron: STEP_Nm_20_12 (claim CH20A-05)', 'exam': "the exam's meribah_case rows on the sentence (Shabbat 55b; Yoma 86b-87a)"}
